WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.030
It has been a while.

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.900
Mother, it is Kageto.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.400
Is everyone well?

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.980
Lately, I have been feeling rather tired.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.540
Why, you ask?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.250
It is because of that Kanmuri guy...

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.960
Even though he is the newest person on the team,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.000
he, along with the manager,
does not work at all.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.390
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.310
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.640
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.000
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.240
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.950
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.800
The world pays attention!!

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.980
The Monaco Cup finals begin!

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.710
You fool!

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.600
We, the French representatives, placed
a bet with the Japanese representatives

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:37.070
that the team with the lower score in
the second preliminary would withdraw.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:39.220
And, of all things for you to draw...

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.910
That is a complete disgrace, Edward.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.720
My deepest apologies.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:50.660
The French representatives must not disgrace themselves any further in the Monaco Cup.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:54.230
It seems that it’s finally time for us to become whole.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.990
A-Anything but that!

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.350
There’s no use arguing about it!

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:06.100
No!

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.770
There we go.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.300
Yo. I made you wait, did I not?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:22.030
Well then, I will now announce the 16 teams

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.300
who have won the right to
participate in the Monaco Cup Finals.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.700
It’s finally here.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.660
Yeah.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.310
First, those with the full 10 points.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.210
France.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:37.110
Likewise, with a perfect score, America.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.590
Great!

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.320
Wonderful!

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.920
Followed by England, China and Egypt.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.710
Huh? He’s...

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.170
Followed by England, China and Egypt.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.820
You have all passed the preliminaries too!

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.330
And now, those who passed with 8 points...

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.260
He’s...

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.830
Japon!

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:53.850
Congratulations to the Japanese!

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.590
Th-Thank you....

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.270
Hey, Azuma...

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.650
If there’s only this many Pierrots around,

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.780
doesn’t it remind you of something closer to home?

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.610
Right?

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.030
You think so?

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.100
I don’t really...

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.600
Huh? Someone’s talking about me?

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:12.240
But, really...

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.210
Now, the championship’s pretty much ours, right?

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.620
France wasn’t anything special, either.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.090
That’s inexcusable, Japanese representative.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.250
This is our true form.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.390
What have you done?!

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.640
It’s a three-tiered form!

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.000
It’s a three-tiered form now!

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.900
We both got a full score in the second preliminary.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.650
In the end, it was a draw.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.010
I’m appalled at your having said
that France isn’t anything special.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.150
You’re a moron.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.510
Although we both had perfect scores,
Japan has the Ebisu points.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.080
With the Ebisu points, it’s our victory.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.290
Stop it, Kawachi.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.460
Suwabara?

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.750
I’ll forget the matter of the preliminary.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:01.490
Next time, bring it on from the front,
without playing any dirty tricks.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.490
With that, we may be able to
have somewhat of a decent match.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.530
“Somewhat of a decent”...
You impudent little...

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.770
Next time, I’ll be sure to make you
regret having made us into this form.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.100
What is it, Suwabara?

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.770
Why have pity on people like that?

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.900
Didn’t you notice it?

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:24.900
Huh?

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.560
Just now, the third son’s mask was slightly crooked.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:30.720
I’m sure that he’s being punished badly inside.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.330
You even lost in the argument!

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.770
Stop it!

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:38.960
It was just really pitiful.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.270
I guess those siblings don’t get along too well.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.010
Hey, Kawachi...

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.780
It’s been bothering me for a while,
but he’s...

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.280
He’s that guy... um...

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.800
Oh, it’s Shachihoko!

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:53.040
The guy who fought with you at
the Pantasia newcomers’ battle.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:53.890
Oh yeah!

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:55.150
It’s Shachihoko!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.460
Hey! Shachihoko!

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:00.600
Huh?

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.480
Azuma!

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.940
It was bothering me a little
that you hadn’t noticed me at all.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:08.820
Why, you could have just said hello.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.240
Hey, wait a moment.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:12.160
Why are you over here?

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.600
Right now, I’m participating as an American
representative on behalf of St. Pierre’s US branch.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.690
S-St. Pierre?!

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:20.440
What does this mean?

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.590
Since you’re originally an American, I understand
why you’re an American representative...

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.670
But, why St. Pierre?

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.950
The granddaughter of Pantasia’s owner, Yukino-san...

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.470
She offered to introduce me
to the US branch of St. Pierre,

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.410
and asked if I wanted to enter the Monaco Cup.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.980
Y-Yukino did?!

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:45.610
I didn’t quite understand why Yukino-san knew the owner of St. Pierre, her business rival,

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:48.670
but for me, it was a heaven-sent chance.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:52.570
If it meant being able to fight Azuma
once more, I’d have taken anything on.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:53.680
Shachihoko...

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.160
Get ready, Azuma.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.370
I’ve worked hard since then.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.750
I’ve become much stronger than I was before.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.830
The other two American representatives

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:07.500
are also great artisans personally selected from around the world by St. Pierre’s manager.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:09.190
They’re so strong, they’ll shock you.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:12.950
The championship is... ours!

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.470
That’s not going to happen, Shachihoko.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:17.480
We won’t lose either!

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:21.020
I’m looking forward to our match.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:21.960
Yeah.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.190
Well, see ya.
Let’s meet again at the finals.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.320
Yep, yep.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:34.910
I see.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.690
That guy from the Pantasia Nagoya Branch
is participating at the Monaco Cup, is he?

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.410
What do you think?

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:44.330
Why did Yukino send Shachihoko here?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.210
She probably noticed that we’ve begun to move,

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:50.960
and prepared a strong opponent to
defeat the Japanese representatives.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:56.430
It appears that the American representatives have
been sent by them to eliminate the Japanese team.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:57.200
What was that?!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.430
St. Pierre’s owner is a fearsome man.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.270
It wouldn’t surprise me if he figured out

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:08.480
that I’m thinking of protecting Pantasia
with the money we earn, in the Monaco Cup.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.610
So, you’re saying that he’s reading all of our moves?

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.230
Yes.

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.220
You’re kidding!

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.770
Well, what can we do?!

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.320
Calm down, Kawachi-san!

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.080
At any rate, we must win.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.100
Whether or not he’s figured it out,
there’s no other path for you to take.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:26.960
That’s true...

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.130
Very well.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.860
We have no choice but to win.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:35.110
Exactly.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.470
Either way, no matter who comes along...

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:40.120
you just have to win the matches.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.620
In fact, the people in real trouble might be...

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:47.070
us, the members of the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.660
Ten million yen has been
withdrawn from Kanmuri’s bank account.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.580
Is that so?

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.410
That’s pretty impressive.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.890
How’d you know that he
would begin to make his move?

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.580
It’s simple.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:06.900
He currently has no other way
of exacting his revenge on you.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:08.800
Revenge, eh?

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:11.610
A rather cute little thing he’s trying there.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:15.880
By the way, are we all right?

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.610
That kid from Nagoya prefecture...

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:23.720
He lost to the cockroach in only the second round of the Pantasia newcomers’ battle.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.330
No way!

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:30.800
He seems to have lost in that
match because of the yakisoba he made.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.800
He’s the California State
Bread Guild Examination Champion.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.780
His skills as a baker are first class.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.810
He’s not a man who’d be finished at just yakisoba.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:43.120
Is that so?

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:44.810
If so, I guess I can relax, eh?

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:48.330
More importantly, what do we have on Tsukino-kun?

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.940
Has she invested in this as well?

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.330
Yeah.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:55.190
She seems to have invested most of
the Southern Tokyo Branch’s capital into it.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:09:59.880
All right.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.200
This is when we attack.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:03.300
It’s me.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.580
Connect me to the manager.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:06.470
This is Kazamori, the manager.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:11.020
Reduce the prices on all items at
St. Pierre’s Main Branch by 70%.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:12.900
You can call it whatever you like.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.200
You can call it a “thank you to our customers” sale.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.590
But why all of a sudden...?

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.610
Any more questions, and you’ll be fired.

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:21.100
Very well.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:25.280
Starting right now, all items
are to be sold at a 70% discount.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.100
Hurry up!

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.080
The Southern Tokyo Branch currently has zero capital.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.290
We should be able to crush them in a week.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:39.610
And next, if we take over Pantasia’s Main Branch...

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:43.270
On top of losing at the Monaco Cup...

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:47.520
the Japanese representatives will no
longer even have a place to return to.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.280
It looks like things are going to get interesting.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.440
Everyone, we’re in trouble!

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:13.440
St. Pierre’s Main. Branch is
having a big 70% discount sale!

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:22.450
J-Just when we’d begun to have more
customers thanks to the Black <i>Japan</i>...

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.450
We are in a pinch, Mother.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.430
So that’s how they want to play after all, eh?

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:28.760
What do you mean, “after all”?

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:33.310
St. Pierre has figured out that we invested the store’s capital into the Monaco Cup.

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:36.960
In order to not lose this opportunity,
they’ve attacked our store full force.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.070
No way...

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:43.650
While the Southern Tokyo Branch may
have been a little in the red up until now...

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:49.450
so far, we’ve gotten by with the financial
assistance Tsukino-san receives from the owner.

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:53.650
However, now that we’ve invested
those funds into the Monaco Cup...

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.340
If we increase our deficit any further,
we’ll have no choice but to shut down.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:02.130
I’ll tell Grandfather everything honestly,
and get us some financial aid.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:03.410
Don’t say stupid things!

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:06.680
Do that and see what happens.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.800
Even if you manage to raise the money,

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.720
you’ll be labeled “the granddaughter
who frittered the store’s funds away,”

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.790
and lose in the battle for the next successor!

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:16.000
And that would be exactly what Yukino wants!

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.320
So... what can we do?

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:26.510
Th-Th-This is embarrassing...

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.990
This is great, Matsushiro-san!

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:31.660
It’s a great idea to have a
demonstration sale for our bread.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:35.670
It’s been adopted by first-class
department stores as an effective tactic.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:41.040
Anyway, we’re unique in having one person
who’s able to do multiple sales at the same time.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.210
Yep.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:44.030
This guy’s amazing.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.040
If we count the one at the register, I wonder how many of Kinoshita-san there are...

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:50.350
It’s really amazing.

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:53.470
How can he clone himself?

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:56.100
The Kinoshita Circus is very famous in Japan.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:56.890
Huh?

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:57.550
Actually...

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:03.690
he’s the son of the Great Kinoshita Circus family!

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:06.030
So he can do at least that much, of course.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:12.120
The sons of distinguished circus
families can clone themselves these days?

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.060
I didn’t know that...

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:14.880
It’s common sense.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.870
Why did the son of such a
distinguished family become a baker?

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:22.090
Once, while he was at a baking
class sponsored by Pantasia...

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.840
Tsukino lured him with her charms.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.800
Lured him?

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:25.710
It was a sure kill.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.670
Amazing!
It was a sure kill.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:27.920
You learn really quickly!

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.050
You have great potential!

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:30.320
I see...

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.350
...is what I want to say,

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:34.390
but there’s just one thing I’m worried about.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:35.310
What is it?

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:38.330
Usually, preparing the dough in the
morning is the only thing we do together.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.150
Everyone
Usually, preparing the dough in the
morning is the only thing we do together.

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:40.840
Everyone

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:42.850
However, in the demonstration sale,

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:43.340
he has to start from the preparation of the dough on his own.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.650
Him

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:48.590
He’s even making my pan au algue.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:51.570
I wonder if it tastes all right...

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:52.810
Here.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.290
Pan au algue, Kinoshita-style.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:56.310
Eat it and see.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.550
Three years ago,

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.360
I was still a student at Harvard.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.530
That’s right, it felt just like this.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:23.630
I’d always caress your silky
hair softly with my left hand,

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:26.960
and with my right hand,
I’d gently put pressure on your nape.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:28.630
And...

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:30.720
a gentle kiss...

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:37.990
F-For some reason, the
images from some strange drama,

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:39.900
where I take on the role of Kuroyanagi-senpai’s lover,

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.150
are flowing into my brain!

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:45.150
Stop it, please!

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:50.160
So, how was it?

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:54.270
It’s not exactly the same as mine, but...

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:58.170
It’s 95% similar to the original bread.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.850
So, now you understand, right?

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.670
He can’t make an original bread at all, but...

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.990
He’s a genius at copying!

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:14.430
Once he’s seen it, he can make the
same bread with an accuracy of above 95%.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.210
Th-That’s amazing...

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.440
S-So, from now onwards...

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:24.510
we can just have Kinoshita-san knead
the dough in the morning as well, right?

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.440
You’re right!

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.130
I didn’t think of that...

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.550
Just as you’d expect of Harvard.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.340
Not at all...

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.950
They’re saying whatever they like again...

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.700
Here’s some tea, Kinoshita-san.

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:43.190
I’ll leave it here.

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.020
Here you go.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:46.270
Tsukino-san!

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:48.570
That’s right.

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:53.540
No matter how badly I’m treated,
as long as I can stay close to Tsukino-san...

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:56.990
Oh, it’s almost time for
“It’s All Right to Laugh.”

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:59.160
I’ll leave the rest to you!

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.930
Tsukino-san...

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.170
These days, I’m laughing at jokes like this.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:10.420
You think I’m getting old?

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.460
Azuma-kun...

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:12.800
Kawachi-san...

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.450
We’re somehow managing to hang on over here.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:20.230
So, please aim for the championship and do your best.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.470
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:36.010
And now, I wish to begin the finals of the Monaco Cup.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:38.410
For the first day of the finals,

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:42.020
we have prepared a special task suitable for you,

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.970
who have made it to the top 16 spots in the world!

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.080
The first task is...

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:49.250
a speed contest.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:52.530
Make a delicious bread faster than anyone else, please.

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:53.920
What was that?!

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:55.030
A speed contest?!

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:59.530
The top eight teams to make
their bread the fastest will pass.

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:01.530
Very well, then... start!

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.770
So, we just have to make it fast?

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.560
So it seems...

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.440
Why are you saying this so calmly?!

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:08.750
Just panic a little, will you?

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:13.070
A delicious bread is made by
allowing it to ferment slowly.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:17.510
It’s impossible to make a bread that
can satisfy that Pierrot in a short time.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.450
But, we can always make it
without fermenting it, you know...

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:21.260
Exactly.

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.830
Th-That’s right!

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:29.110
Azuma’s <i>Japan</i>s had among them <i>Japan</i> #16,
which was made without fermentation.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.110
I forgot to say this, but...

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.860
With that, even in a short period of time, we couldn’t...

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:35.570
This time, we will not accept
breads that are not fermented.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:41.000
I mean, if not for that rule, you would
all just make non-fermented breads, right?

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.680
What can we do?

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:45.600
Kawachi.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:48.140
There’s no need to panic so much.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:49.310
What was that?!

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:51.020
It’s a strict rule,

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:52.840
but we’re all under the same circumstances.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:58.610
In that case, since all of us possess
either Solar Gauntlets or Solar Hands,

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:01.850
we, the Japanese representatives,
have a great advantage here.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.740
Exactly, Kawachi.

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:04.740
I see...

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:05.830
That’s true...

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.160
All right!

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.060
Since that’s settled...

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.060
Let’s start kneading it right away!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:15.820
Initiating, Solar Gauntlets!!

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:21.560
Solar Gauntlet Overcoat!

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:24.330
Solar... Hands.

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:26.830
Come to think of it, I’ve
forgotten to say one more thing...

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:29.850
Next, if we just increase the amount of yeast we use...

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:32.340
Adding the time for the first and second fermentations, as well as the baking...

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.930
In just 90 minutes...

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:34.920
We can be done!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.320
The time limit is 60 minutes.

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.180
If you’re late, you will automatically be disqualified.

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:43.180
Hey, what was that?!

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:47.330
Also, while this is a competition to select eight teams,

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:49.660
if only one team clears this task,

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:51.690
that team will automatically
become the champion, no hard feelings.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.190
You there! Seriously, cut the crap!

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:57.170
How can you forget to say something that important?

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:58.190
I’m sorry.

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:01.590
But even clowns forget things occasionally.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:02.200
Also...

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.700
The other countries are working
at it without getting agitated.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:09.710
This is unsightly, Japanese representative.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.520
In the end, the Monaco Cup’s a world tournament.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:14.900
If your answer to the task of making bread quickly is

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:16.860
“We’re all right if we can make it without fermentation,”

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:18.570
or “We’re all right if we have 90 minutes”...

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:22.930
If your skills are on that low a level, then
it’s best for you to forfeit from the very start.

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:26.320
You’re talking big to me when your head’s all slanted?

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:29.290
It’s not the time to be answering
to their provocation, Kawachi.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.200
If the time limit is 60 minutes,

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.830
then we don’t have more than around 45 minutes.

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:35.290
We’ll really be disqualified.

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:36.500
Th-That’s right...

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.090
Let’s hurry up, Suwabara.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:39.390
Azuma, let’s hurry up!

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:40.710
Old... Mister Pierrot...

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:41.510
Azuma...?
Old... Mister Pierrot...

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:42.950
Old... Mister Pierrot...

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.560
He can’t be complaining to Pierrot, can he?

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.320
No, that can’t be it.

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:54.190
He said that there was something that he needed.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:55.940
He probably went to ask for that.

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:56.710
Is that so?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:01.220
But, we don’t even have 45 minutes anymore...

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:05.330
Azuma, we can only depend on you now.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:17.460
CS is broadcasting the finals of the Monaco Cup live.

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.150
Yeah, that’s because the Monaco
Cup’s taking place at the casino.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.340
The matches start in the evening over there.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:27.160
Since Japan is at the opposite end of the earth, it’s broadcast in the morning here.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:31.410
And we can see the crushing of the cockroaches, live.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:33.060
Yeah...

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:34.120
But...

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:42.440
What do we do about this mushroom-head
who’s multiplying like a creepy-crawly?

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:44.840
His capacity for reproduction
is truly like that of a cockroach.

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:48.660
At this rate, we won’t be able to
crush the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:54.810
I hadn’t calculated for the Southern Tokyo
Branch having those kinds of troops in reserve.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:59.710
Also, it seems that this particular employee has been with them for about two years,

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:02.970
but until the other day, I hadn’t
even noticed his very existence.

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:05.560
Me neither.

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:09.640
But, we can’t really laugh here.

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:13.180
At this rate, far from us crushing them,
they’ll take away the customers, too.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:14.820
We don’t have to worry about that.

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:18.270
It’s true that people are gathering there,

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:22.710
but that demonstration isn’t
really raising their sales by much.

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:24.320
Far from it,

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:28.360
people who wish to eat bread after watching the demonstration are coming over to us.

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:31.580
Even if we can’t crush them, we don’t have
to worry about them stealing our customers.

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:32.780
Why?

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:34.740
Could it be that his stuff tastes bad?

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:37.580
No, it seems it tastes pretty good, too.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.800
Although, I guess... it’s his character.

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:45.010
I guess no one in particular would
want to eat the bread that he makes.

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:46.170
Being human...

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:48.630
You’d kinda feel sorry for the guy.

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:49.850
Yeah.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:54.910
Mother, for some reason, I feel that
someone truly awful is pitying me...

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:56.920
I can’t stand to watch it.

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:03.610
What is it?

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:06.380
That kid...

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:09.120
He noticed <i>that</i>, eh?

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:13.640
The Japanese representatives are better than I thought.

00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:14.890
Huh?

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:18.050
I’m flying to Monaco.

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:23.630
Mother, nobody knew that on this day...

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:31.180
the doors to a truly cold fate for Azuma were opened.

00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:07.430
All right, it’s a speed contest.

00:24:07.430 --> 00:24:09.090
Although it may be a speed contest,

00:24:09.090 --> 00:24:11.430
it’s crazy to ask us to make bread in 60 minutes!

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:13.220
All right, it’s a speed contest!

00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:14.140
Yay!

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:15.350
And you’re not listening!

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:16.670
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.670 --> 00:24:17.540
A speed contest!!

00:24:17.540 --> 00:24:18.750
<i>Ping</i> it with that!

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:19.890
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.340 --> 00:24:22.640
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:25.300
The word “circus” originates
from the Latin word “circus.”

00:24:25.300 --> 00:24:27.680
It means “circle,” or “to revolve.”

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:31.660
If it’s a circular stage, then you have 360° vision, and you can see well from any seat, right?

00:24:32.060 --> 00:24:33.860
Really?!
